# An unterminated string ending in `\`: just adding a quote would leave it open, so the help doubles the backslash.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where p == 'abc\
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..25
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..25
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..25
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "p"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        EQ2@17..19 "=="
        WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
        LITERAL@20..25
          STRING@20..25 "'abc\\"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0002]: unterminated string
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from t | where p == 'abc\
  |                     ^^^^^ this string is never closed
  |
  = help: the `\` at the end escapes a quote; to end the string with a backslash, double it and add a closing `'`
  = note: a string ends at the end of its line
